{
  "about": "Battle Sim move effects, read by BattleMoveEffects. Keys are move names normalized by BattleSimSeed.normalize (lowercase letters and digits only: \"Swords Dance\" is swordsdance). Values name effects the engine already implements, so a move works from a line here only if it uses one of them. Stats are atk, def, spAtk, spDef, speed; stages are [stat, change] pairs. Lists that route moves to hand-written code (tier 3 and 5 status moves, fixed-damage moves, damage modifiers) stay in BattleSimulator.swift, since a line here alone wouldn't do anything.",
  "notes": {
    "first_turn_only": "Fail after the user's first action since switching in (Fake Out, First Impression).",
    "stat_changes": "Status moves that change stat stages: target is self or opponent.",
    "status_inflicts": "Status moves that inflict a status condition: burn, paralysis, poison, toxic, sleep, freeze.",
    "confusion_inflicts": "Status moves that confuse the target. Swagger and Flatter's stat boost is in code.",
    "weather_setters": "Moves that set weather: sun, rain, sand, snow.",
    "terrain_setters": "Moves that set terrain: electric, grassy, misty, psychic.",
    "hazard_setters": "Moves that set an entry hazard: stealthRock, spikes, stickyWeb, toxicSpikes.",
    "protect_family": "Protect variants. The shared logic is applyProtectFamily; a variant's contact effect is in protectContactEffect.",
    "pivot_moves": "Moves that switch the user out: damage = only when the move connected; force = always.",
    "screen_setters": "light, reflect, aurora (needs snow), safeguard. 5 turns, 8 with Light Clay.",
    "room_setters": "trickRoom, wonderRoom, magicRoom, gravity. 5 turns.",
    "hazard_removers": "ownSide (Rapid Spin), bothSides (Defog), tidyUp (also removes screens), mortalSpin (also poisons foes).",
    "ohko_moves": "One-hit KO moves, with the level-based accuracy formula.",
    "trap_moves": "Damaging moves that trap the target on hit.",
    "ballistic_moves": "Blocked by Bulletproof.",
    "sound_moves": "Blocked by Soundproof.",
    "contact_moves": "Contact fallback for when MoveData.makesContact is unreliable; contact is makesContact or listed here.",
    "charge_moves": "Two-turn moves. {user} in charge_log is the user's name. skip_in_weather skips the charge turn; invulnerability is underground, airborne, underwater or vanished.",
    "invulnerability_exceptions": "Moves that can hit a semi-invulnerable target, by kind.",
    "invulnerability_double_damage": "Of those, the ones that deal double damage.",
    "multi_hit_fallback": "[min, max] hits, for moves whose synced data lacks them.",
    "secondary_effects": "On-hit effects when the target survives. chance is the printed percent.",
    "self_stat_changes_on_hit": "Stat changes the user always takes after a damaging hit."
  },
